- src/services/contentstack.ts :: options — This is the Contentstack SDK initialization config where `live_preview` settings must be added to enable draft/preview content delivery. The `contentstack.Stack(options)` call at line 91 is the single point where the SDK client is created — Live Preview requires a `live_preview` key in this config object, and all downstream data fetching (getEntry, ContentstackFactory) flows through this Stack instance.
- src/context/contentstackContext.tsx :: ContentstackContext — The React context that provides Contentstack content to all components via `useContent`. When Live Preview pushes updates, the context value must be refreshed reactively so every component reading from `useContent()` re-renders with the new draft data. This is the consumer-side attachment point — the context provider wrapper must subscribe to Contentstack Live Preview events and update its value.


